Binary sensor packet protocol:

[TYPE][PAYLOAD]

TYPE     uint8_t

where:
  TYPE     - packet type identifier
  PAYLOAD  - raw sensor data interpreted according to TYPE

Current TYPEs:
  TYPE           CODE

  LIDAR          0x54
  ACCEL          0x67



LIDAR binary packet protocol:

- Data Length: 1 byte (upper 3 bits reserved, lower 5 bits = number of points, fixed 12)
- Radar speed: 2 bytes (deg/s)
- Start angle: 2 bytes (0.01 degree)
- DataPoints: 3 bytes each point (distanceValue: 2 bytes, confidence: 1 byte)
- End angle: 2 bytes (0.01 degree)
- Timestamp: 2 bytes (ms, wraps at 30000)
- CRC8: 1 byte checksum

ACCEL (Accelerometer) binary packet protocol:

- Magnitude X:   2 bytes
- Magnitude Y:   2 bytes
- Magnitude Z:   2 bytes
- RHALL:         2 bytes
- Gyroscope X:   2 bytes
- Gyroscope Y:   2 bytes
- Gyroscope Z:   2 bytes
- Acceleration X: 2 bytes
- Acceleration Y: 2 bytes
- Acceleration Z: 2 bytes

TOTAL PAYLOAD SIZE: 20 bytes
